"lines": [
"One hole on a Canadian island has swallowed two centuries of treasure hunts.",
"Diggers said they hit a log platform every ten feet.",
"Some were topped with charcoal, putty, even coconut fiber.",
"At ninety feet, a flat stone carved with strange symbols.",
"Then something hard at ninety-eight feet. By morning, the pit held sixty feet of water.",
"A young Franklin Roosevelt dug here too.",
"In 1971, a camera went down a shaft about 235 feet deep. None of what crews claimed to see was ever confirmed.",
"But geologists say the Money Pit may be a natural sinkhole, and the logs, fallen trees.",
"And the carved stone? The only drawing of its symbols dates from 1949.",
"Still, no treasure has ever come out of it.",
"Nobody explained it."
